---
import MetaChecker from '../components/MetaChecker.astro';
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ToolSeoSections from '../components/ToolSeoSections.astro';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Meta Title & Description Checker — Preview SEO snippets | Bizzon"
  description="Free browser-based Meta Title & Description Checker by Bizzon. Measure title and meta description length, preview snippets, and improve basic SEO copy without uploading text."
  canonicalPath="/meta-title-description-checker"
  heading="Meta Title & Description Checker"
  intro="Measure SEO title and meta description length, see a simple Google-style preview, and get quick guidance before publishing a page."
>
  <MetaChecker />
  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Check snippet length</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Count title and meta description characters as you type, with simple guidance for common SEO length ranges.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Private by default</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Your text stays in your browser. Bizzon does not upload or store your SEO drafts, titles, or descriptions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">Useful for publishing</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Prepare search snippets for blog posts, landing pages, product pages, documentation, and utility pages.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm md:p-8" aria-labelledby="seo-title-checker-guide">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-blue-700">SEO snippet guide</p>
    <h2 id="seo-title-checker-guide" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black text-slate-950">How to check an SEO title</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-slate-600">Use this SEO title checker to draft a clear search-result title, then check whether the wording explains the page before you focus on character count. A good title matches the page topic, puts the useful detail first, and gives searchers a reason to open the result.</p>
    <ol class="mt-6 grid gap-3 text-slate-700 md:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-4"><strong>1. Name the page topic.</strong> Start with the product, question, tool, or guide someone is looking for.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-4"><strong>2. Add a useful detail.</strong> Explain what the page helps people do instead of repeating a keyword.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-4"><strong>3. Check the preview.</strong> Use the title length and Google-style preview as practical guidance, not a strict promise.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-4"><strong>4. Keep it honest.</strong> The title should describe the page visitors actually reach after clicking.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 md:p-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Meta title vs page title</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">A page title or H1 is the main heading people see on the page. A meta title, often called an SEO title, is the title sent to search engines and usually shown as the blue link in a result. They can be the same, but they do not have to be. Use a meta title checker to make sure both still describe the same page clearly.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-blue-50 p-6 md:p-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">How to write a meta description</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">A meta description should explain the page benefit in plain language. Include the topic naturally, add the specific task or outcome, and avoid repeating the same phrase. Google may rewrite snippets, so prioritize a helpful sentence rather than chasing an exact character count.</p><p class="mt-4"><a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/how-to-write-meta-descriptions">Read the meta description writing guide →</a></p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm md:p-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">SEO title and meta description examples</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-rose-100 bg-rose-50 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-rose-700">Too vague</p><p class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold text-slate-950">Best SEO Tool</p><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">It does not say what the tool checks or why a searcher should choose it.</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-emerald-700">Clearer title</p><p class="mt-3 text-lg font-bold text-slate-950">SEO Title Checker — Preview title length and snippets</p><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">It names the job and tells the searcher what happens after they click.</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-rose-100 bg-rose-50 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-rose-700">Too broad description</p><p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">Learn about coffee</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-emerald-700">Clearer description</p><p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950">Coffee brewing guide: methods, ratios, and beginner tips</p></div></div><p class="mt-6 text-slate-700">Need more room for a draft? Use the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/character-counter">Character Counter</a>, then compare practical ranges in the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/meta-description-length-guide">Meta Description Length Guide</a>.</p></section>
  <section class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-blue-50 p-6 md:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Related SEO and text tools</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-700">Need a clean URL too? Try the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/slug-generator">Slug Generator</a>. Need to measure draft length? Use the <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/character-counter">Character Counter</a> or <a class="font-bold text-blue-700" href="/word-counter">Word Counter</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <ToolSeoSections slug="meta-title-description-checker" />
</ToolLayout>
